nsi, nsiproxy.sys: Work without routing sockets.

iOS has no routing socket or kernel event socket, so nsiproxy skips
them (WINE_IOS_NO_ROUTE_SOCKET, WINE_NSI_KEV_EVENTS), reports an empty
route table and stubs if_get_physical. nsi calls nsiproxy in-process
when there is no \\.\Nsi device; 11-wine-ios.sh installs nsiproxy.so
as nsi.so for that.

The in-process fallback is adapted from Madeira's Wine fork
(willfaust/wine d3d5a179a5, and 5c4d1f7a6f by 125hz).
---
diff --git a/dlls/nsi/nsi.c b/dlls/nsi/nsi.c
index 14be842871a9e9a205c52a530ab62d8423ac7afb..7546dd1cf283e730cc02959874ab2f9295e7fd3a 100644
--- a/dlls/nsi/nsi.c
